<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">Section 19 of the LLP Act, 2008</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>S.19(1):</strong> LLP may change name by filing notice with ROC in prescribed form and fees. <strong>S.19(2):</strong> If name identical/too similar to existing entity: change by ordinary resolution. <strong>S.19(3):</strong> Central Government can direct name change if against public interest.</p><p><strong>Rule 20(1):</strong> Procedure — RUN-LLP reservation + Form 5 filing + ROC approval.</p><p>Name must end with "Limited Liability Partnership" or "LLP". LLPIN does NOT change — same entity, new name. Patron manages complete process for Delhi LLPs.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for LLP Name Change in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>RUN-LLP:</strong> Name reservation. Rs 200. Valid 3 months. Up to 2 names. One resubmission if rejected.</p><p><strong>Form 5:</strong> Notice of name change. ROC within 30 days of RUN-LLP. Designated partner DSC.</p><p><strong>Fresh Certificate:</strong> New COI with new name. Effective from certificate date. Same LLPIN.</p><p><strong>Form 3:</strong> Updated agreement. Within 30 days of certificate. Delhi stamp paper Rs 100-200.</p>

